      "math_academy_id": "e-5519",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^3 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2,$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14136609/assets/2f52df9d240ea0b583cb3ae40281ef601b496644cd335eb73fb26cc5461dcc77.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
